<attribute name="mainDescription" nodeId="750b654e">&lt;p&gt;
    A survey is a research tool consisting of a series of questions used to gather information from the client. Similar to
    interviewing and workshops, the survey will be analyzed to provide better insight on the client&apos;s current state.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="externalId" nodeId="b9f44b7e"></attribute>
<attribute name="keyConsiderations" nodeId="c1fd7fe2">&lt;p&gt;
    There are various types of survey questions and ways of collecting the information:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Open-ended - free form text, short answer/essay
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Close-ended - multiple choices
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Partial opened - multiple choice with other options
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Scaled
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Ranking
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="longPresentationName" nodeId="b5d81e25"></attribute>
<attribute name="purpose" nodeId="f47d464b">&lt;p&gt;
    To gather a list of targeted questions that will be used to gather specific information related to the objectives of
    the project.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
